linkers. We demonstrate that, with increased net positive charge in the cationic metal center, such zwitterionic MOFs exhibit enhanced catalytic activities for three representative organic transformations, that is, the $\left[2{+}1\right]$ cycloisomerization of enynes, the $\left[3+2\right]$ cycloaddition of aziridines and alkenes, and the $[4^{+2}]$ hetero-Diels-Alder cycloaddition of aldehydes with dienes. Due to the increased Lewis acidity of the porphyrin metal center, the zwitterionic MOFs indeed afford higher reaction yields as well as an improved chemo-, and/or regioselectivity in all three reactions.
## RESULTS AND DISCUSSION
Ligand and MOFs Synthesis. Using the extended octatopic ligand TBCPPP (tetrakis-3,5-bis((4-carboxy)- phenyl)phenyl-porphyrin) developed in our group,13 we first synthesized TBCPPP- $\mathbf{\cdot}\mathbf{Mn}^{\mathrm{III}}\mathbf{Cl}$ and $-\mathrm{Fe}^{\mathrm{III}}\mathrm{Cl}$ linkers (Figure 1a) (See Supporting Information for detailed synthetic procedure). Anion metathesis with $\mathrm{AgBF}_{4}$ was then employed to replace the strongly (S) coordinated $\mathrm{Cl}^{-}$ with weakly (W) coordinated $\mathrm{BF}_{4}^{-}$ . The subsequent solvothermal reaction of octatopic TBCPPP- $\cdot\mathrm{M}\mathrm{\bar{n}^{\mathrm{III}}[\mathrm{BF}_{4}]}$ and - $\mathrm{Fe}^{\mathrm{III}}[\mathrm{BF}_{4}]$ ligands with $\left.\mathrm{In}(\mathrm{NO}_{3})_{3}\right.$ resulted in noncoordinating (N) UNLPF- $\cdot\mathbf{1}4^{-}\mathbf{M}\mathbf{n}^{\mathrm{{III}^{-}}}$ II and UNLPF-16-FeIII, respectively. We also prepared the following MOFs as controls for the catalytic studies (vide infra): (1) UNLPF$13^{-}\mathrm{{Mn}^{\mathrm{{III}}}\mathrm{{Cl}}}$ and UNLPF- $15^{-}\mathrm{Fe}^{\mathrm{III}}\mathrm{Cl}$ using TBCPPP- $\mathbf{\cdotM^{\mathrm{III}}C l}$ linkers $(\mathbf{M}=\mathbf{M}\mathbf{n}$ and Fe) (Figure 1a); (2) neutral metalloporphyrinic MOFs $\mathrm{PCN-}223\mathrm{\overline{{{-}}M n}^{I I I}C l}$ and $P C_{\bf N-22}\bf{3-}\mathrm{Fe^{III}C l}$ using tetratopic TCPP- $\cdot\mathrm{{M}^{\mathrm{{III}}}\mathrm{{Cl}}}$ linkers $\mathrm{(TCPP\I)}=$ tetrakis $\cdot4^{-}$ carboxyphenyl)-porphyrin, $\mathbf{M}=\mathbf{M}\mathbf{n}$ and Fe); and $\left(3\right)$ PCN$223\mathrm{-Mn}^{\mathrm{\bar{III}}}[\mathrm{Sb}\dot{\mathrm{F_{6}}}]$ and $\mathrm{PCN-223\mathrm{-Fe^{III}[B F_{4}]}}$ via post-synthetic anion metathesis with $\mathrm{\AgSbF_{6}}$ and $\mathrm{AgBF}_{4},$ respectively (reported by Zhou et al14) (Figure 1b).
Single crystal X-ray diffraction structural analysis revealed that UNLPF- $\dot{\bf{\Lambda}}_{13-\mathrm{{Mn}}}\mathrm{{^{III}}}\mathrm{{Cl}}$ , UNLPF- $\mathbf{\cdot14^{-Mn}}^{\mathrm{III}}$ , UNLPF$15\mathrm{-Fe}^{\mathrm{III}}\mathrm{Cl}.$ , and UNLPF- $\cdot16\mathrm{-Fe}^{\mathrm{III}}$ crystallize in the same orthorhombic Pnnm space group and are isostructures of UNLPF-10 (Supporting Information, Table $S_{1^{-}4}\dot{}$ ). A chloride anion was crystallographically located on the porphyrin metal centers in the case of UNLPF- ${\bf\cdot}{\bf{1}}3{\bf-}{\bf{M}}{\bf{n}}^{\mathrm{{III}}}\mathrm{{Cl}}$ and -15- $\mathrm{Fe}^{\mathrm{III}}\mathrm{Cl}.$ , with $\mathbf{M}^{\mathrm{III...}}\mathbf{Cl}$ distances of $2.16\mathring{\mathrm{A}}$ and $2.20\mathring\mathrm{A}$ , respectively (Figure $S_{2}$ ). As expected, anion coordination was not present in UNLPF- $\bf{\cdot14^{-M n^{\mathrm{III}}}}$ and $\mathsf{-}\mathsf{1}6\mathsf{-}\mathsf{F e}^{\mathrm{\tiny{III}}}$ . Instead, the coordination of water was observed with $\mathbf{M}^{\mathrm{III...}}\mathbf{O}$ distances of $2.25\mathring\mathrm{A}$ and $2.29\mathring\mathrm{A}$ , respectively, in good agreement with reported values.15 Thorough solvent treatment of UNLPF$\mathbf{14\mathrm{\dot{-}M n}}^{\mathrm{III}}$ and $-\mathbf{16-Fe}^{\mathrm{III}}$ ensured the complete removal of the labile extra-framework $\mathrm{BF}_{4}^{-}$ , evidenced by the absence of the signal of $^{19}\mathrm{F}$ $(\updelta\sim-149\mathrm{\ppm})$ in the ${}^{19}\mathrm{F}$ NMR spectra of acid-digested MOF samples (Figure $S_{4}$ ). The cationic dye uptake analysis13c for UNLPF- $\mathbf{\cdot14^{-Mn}}^{\mathrm{III}}$ and $-\mathbf{16-Fe}^{\mathrm{III}}$ reveals an overall framework charge of $^{\mathfrak{a}}-\mathbf{1}^{\mathfrak{n}}$ per cage, consistent with the average charge occupation of the two $[\mathrm{In}(\mathrm{CO}_{2})_{4}]^{-}$ SBUs and one [MIII-porphyrin]+ center per cage.
The change of coordination environment in the porphyrin metal center resulted from anion metathesis was further confirmed using UV-vis and $\mathrm{\DeltaX}$ -ray photoemission spectroscopy (XPS). Specifically, in the absence of a strongly binding of the chloride ligand, a small blue shift of $5\mathrm{nm}$ and $8\mathrm{nm}$ of the $\mathrm{Q1}$ band of the metalloporphyrin macrocycle in UNLPF- $\mathbf{\cdot14^{-Mn}}^{\mathrm{III}}$ and in -16-FeIII (Figure 2ab), respectively, consistent with the literature values16 as well as the corresponding linkers (Supporting Information, Figure S1). Moreover, the disappearance of the Cl (2p) signal at 201.2 and $_{200.6\mathrm{eV}}$ , respectively (Figure $S{5}\mathrm{\overline{{{\Omega}}}}$ ), as well as the increase of the binding energy of N1s in the XPS spectra (Figure 2c-d) of UNLPF- $\mathbf{\cdot14^{-Mn}}^{\mathrm{{III}}}$ $\langle\Delta\mathrm{BE}=1.30\$ eV) and $-\mathbf{16-Fe}^{\mathrm{III}}$ $\ \mathrm{\Delta}\Delta\mathrm{BE}=1.45\ \mathrm{eV},$ ) also provide experimental proofs of successful preparation of zwitterionic MOF structures that exhibit the complete charge separation of
